# Caddy gets a free HTTPS certificate for your domain automatically.
# Browsers on an https:// game page may only open wss:// (secure) WebSockets, so the relay needs this.
#
#   1. Point a DNS record (e.g. relay.example.com) at your server's IP.
#   2. Run the relay:  PORT=8787 TRUST_PROXY=1 ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://you.github.io node server.js
#   3. Put this file at /etc/caddy/Caddyfile (replace the domain) and reload Caddy.
#
# The game then uses:  wss://relay.example.com/relay

relay.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8787
}
